# Cursor-only extensions — NOT installable in VS Code.
# Install with: `make ext`
# Shared extensions live in Extfile; VS Code equivalents in Extfile.vscode.
#
# Anysphere publishes these forks to OpenVSX to replace Microsoft-proprietary
# extensions that Cursor cannot ship. They are deliberately not on the
# Microsoft Marketplace, so VS Code keeps the ms-* originals instead.

# --- Remote development (Anysphere forks) ---
# SSH remote development (fork of ms-vscode-remote.remote-ssh)
anysphere.remote-ssh
# Dev container support (fork of ms-vscode-remote.remote-containers)
anysphere.remote-containers
# WSL remote development (fork of ms-vscode-remote.remote-wsl)
anysphere.remote-wsl

# --- Language servers ---
# Python type checking (fork of Pylance, which is Microsoft-proprietary)
anysphere.cursorpyright
